# Customer Personality Analysis
## Unsupervised Segmentation + Supervised Classification

A machine learning project that combines KMeans clustering
and XGBoost classification to segment customers into distinct
personality groups and predict which segment a new customer
belongs to — enabling targeted marketing campaigns.

## The Business Problem

Sending the same marketing message to every customer is
expensive and ineffective. Most campaigns get ignored because
they are not relevant to the person receiving them.

This project solves that by finding the natural groups that
already exist in your customer base — based on how they
actually spend, what they buy, how they respond to campaigns,
and what their life looks like — then building a classifier
that can place any new customer into the right group
automatically.

The result: the right message reaches the right customer
from the moment they sign up.

## What Makes This Project Different

Most classification projects start with predefined labels.
This one does not. The target variable does not exist in
the original dataset — it is discovered from the data itself
using KMeans clustering. Only after the natural groups are
found does the supervised learning begin.

This combination of unsupervised plus supervised learning
is how real customer intelligence systems work in production.

## The Dataset

- Source: Customer Personality Analysis — Kaggle
- Customers: 2,240 records
- Features: 29 columns covering demographics, spending
  history, purchase channels, and campaign responses
- No predefined target — segments discovered through clustering

## The Four Customer Segments

| Segment | Customers (Train) | Profile | Marketing Strategy |
|---|---|---|---|
| At Risk | 846 | Previously active, declining engagement | Win-back campaigns, discounts |
| Potential | 473 | Medium income, growing spend | Bundle deals, growth campaigns |
| Low Engagement | 330 | Low spend, rarely responds | Budget offers, light touch |
| High Value | 142 | High income, high spend, campaign-responsive | Premium offers, loyalty rewards |

Key insight: High Value customers are the smallest segment
at roughly 8% of the base — but they are the most responsive
to campaigns and the highest spenders. The 80/20 rule
showing up in real data.

